WHATNOW

What libtam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise it
at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W14


STATE

  Version 0.14.1 on branch dev (the VERSION file is the version's source
  of truth). Follows the tam-idol 0.2.0 standard (W3). Two static
  archives by default: libtam.a, the core, which needs only libc, and
  libtam-portal.a, which needs D-Bus. The optional libtam-display.a and
  libtam-display-session.a are experimental.

  W5 fixes external opener exec error reporting. W6 reviewed libtam
  against every Tamlinux C program (reviews/R2) and wrote the 0.7
  refactor plan (plans/P1), which Fred approved. W7 released 0.9.2:
  the version for a3e0901's hardening and corrected header comments. W8
  released 0.10.0, the breaking core fixes, with every caller migrated.
  W9 released 0.11.0, the shared primitives (tam_proc, tam_io, tam_sock,
  tam_b64 and the path, UTF-8, guard and JSON additions). W10 released
  0.12.0, the terminal stack. W11 released 0.13.0: libtam-render.a,
  holding tam-view's renderer, now shared by tam-view and tam-knox. W12
  released 0.14.0: process options and a secret-safe socket line reader,
  which the migrations need. W13 records the consumer migrations: every
  program that links libtam now uses it (P1 done).

  Recent work: 0.7.0 added the terminal foundation (tam_uni, tam_key,
  tam_tty), used by tam-edit, tam-clam and tam-last; 0.7.1 moved the
  version into VERSION; 0.8.0 retired tam_bundle_guard and added
  tam_cultivar helpers; W2 renamed develop to dev; W3 brought the
  repository up to the tam-idol 0.2.0 standard. W4 defaulted make
  install to ~/.local. Earlier records live in work/history/.

  Plain make install now targets ~/.local and needs no root; an explicit
  PREFIX still wins. tam-last, tam-clam and tam-pane link libtam.a from
  there.


